problems.problem:
Denote by $\mathcal{M}_2(\mathbb{R})$ the set of all $2\times2$ matrices with real entries. Prove that:

a) for every $A\in\mathcal{M}_2(\mathbb{R})$ there exist $B,C\in\mathcal{M}_2(\mathbb{R})$ such that $A=B^2+C^2$;

b) there do not exist $B,C\in\mathcal{M}_2(\mathbb{R})$ such that $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}=B^2+C^2$ and $BC=CB$.
